---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Q1 = `function shout(word) {
  return word + "!";
}

console.log(shout("go"));`;
const Q2 = `function shout(word) {
  console.log(word + "!");
}

let x = shout("go");
console.log(x);`;
const Q3 = `PROCEDURE half(n)
{
  RETURN(n / 2)
}

DISPLAY(half(10))
DISPLAY(half(half(40)))`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 9</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">Six questions &middot; 11 minutes &middot; cumulative</h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>Six exam-style questions covering everything through Activity 2.3, weighted toward <b>procedures and return values</b>. Two are cumulative from Quarter 1.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Set a timer for 11 minutes.</b> Work them out on paper; do not
            run the code. Mark each answer <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>. Guess
            rather than leave a blank.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <p>
            Four have exactly one correct answer, one asks you to select{" "}
            <i>all</i> that apply, and the last is about data or the impact of
            computing rather than about code.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={Q1} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Question 1" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>go</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>go!</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>undefined</code></li>
            <li>(D) Nothing</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={Q2} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Question 2" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>go!</code> then <code>go!</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>undefined</code> only</li>
            <li>(C) An error</li>
            <li>(D) <code>go!</code> then <code>undefined</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={Q3} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Question 3 — exam notation" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>5 20</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>5 5</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>5 10</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>5 40</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4 &mdash; Select all that apply</h3>

          <p>Which of these are true about <code>return</code>?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) It hands a value back to the caller</li>
            <li>(B) It exits the procedure immediately</li>
            <li>(C) Code written after it in the same block still runs</li>
            <li>(D) A procedure with no <code>return</code> hands back <code>undefined</code></li>
            <li>(E) It prints the value to the screen</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5</h3>

          <p>A procedure is defined as <code>function fee(weight, distance)</code>. A student calls <code>fee(200, 5)</code> intending 5 kg over 200 miles. What happens?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) The procedure runs and returns a wrong number, with no warning</li>
            <li>(B) An error, because the arguments are in the wrong order</li>
            <li>(C) JavaScript matches the arguments by name</li>
            <li>(D) The procedure returns <code>undefined</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 6 &mdash; Data and Impact</h3>

          <p>A single byte can represent how many different values?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>8</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>64</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>128</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>256</code></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Six answers, each marked <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>, plus how far
            you got when the timer went off. Worth <b>2 points</b>, graded on
            completion.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
